BT 1 0 0 1 0 56 Tm 13 TL /F1 9 Tf 0 0 0 rg (RESULTS: As PHQ-9 depression severity increased, there was a substantial decrease in functional status on all 6) Tj T* (SF-20 subscales. Also, symptom-related difficulty, sick days, and health care utilization increased. Using the MHP) Tj T* (reinterview as the criterion standard, a PHQ-9 score > or =10 had a sensitivity of 88% and a specificity of 88% for major) Tj T* -0.010184 Tw (depression. PHQ-9 scores of 5, 10, 15, and 20 represented mild, moderate, moderately severe, and severe depression,) Tj T* 0 Tw (respectively. Results were similar in the primary care and obstetrics-gynecology samples.) Tj T* ET
